From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: thisiscamk <100883750+thisiscamk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] block: asp: Take the storage endpoint from the RTKit protocol

The storage endpoint is the first app endpoint, which RTKit 11 and
later number 0x20 but RTKit 10 numbers 0x5 or 0x6. The driver hardcodes
0x20, so it cannot start the iPad Air's ANS, which negotiates RTKit
10.2 on iOS 12 and serves storage on endpoint 6.

Ask RTKit for the first app endpoint instead. The iPad Air 2 (RTKit
12.0) still gets 0x20.

[Orchard: from thisiscamk/ipad-air-j72-linux 2a257d6,
 code/current/kernel/0001-j72-installed-kernel-snapshot.patch
 (drivers/block/asp.c, apple_asp_rtkit_epmap_done()); his J72 run:
 code/storage/linux-asp-observer35/README.md ("negotiated RTKit 10.2,
 endpoint 6").]
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/block/asp.c | 13 ++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/block/asp.c b/drivers/block/asp.c
index ae1cc80ec..2fb7aadff 100644
--- a/drivers/block/asp.c
+++ b/drivers/block/asp.c
@@ -29,7 +29,6 @@
 #include <linux/dmapool.h>
 
 #define DEVICE_NAME	"asp"
-#define ASP_RTKIT_ENDPOINT	0x20
 #define DISK_NAME	"asp%dn%d"
 
 #define AKF_V1_REMAP_AP_LO	0x8
@@ -1177,11 +1176,15 @@ static void apple_asp_rtkit_epmap_done(void *cookie)
 	int ret;
 
 	/*
-	 * The storage endpoint is the first app endpoint: 0x20 on RTKit 11 and
-	 * later (the iPad Air 2's ANS speaks 12.0). Older ANS firmware with
-	 * RTKit 10 is not supported; starting the endpoint fails there.
+	 * The storage endpoint is the first app endpoint: 0x20 on RTKit 11
+	 * and later (the iPad Air 2's ANS speaks 12.0), 0x6 on RTKit 10.2
+	 * (the iPad Air's ANS on iOS 12).
 	 */
-	asp->ep = ASP_RTKIT_ENDPOINT;
+	asp->ep = apple_rtkit_app_ep_to_ep(asp->rtk, 0);
+	if (!asp->ep) {
+		dev_err(asp->dev, "Could not determine the ASP endpoint");
+		return;
+	}
 
 	dev_dbg(asp->dev, "ASP endpoint is %d", asp->ep);
 
